---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import ArchivePanel from "../components/ArchivePanel.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Slyzzed, blue team work, and learning incident response through practical experiments." currentPath="about">
  <main class="page-shell">
    <ArchivePanel
      label="Slyzzed"
      title="About"
      lede="I’m Slyzzed, a cybersecurity professional working on blue teams, with a particular interest in learning and practising incident response."
    >
      <div class="prose-block">
        <p>At work, patching and other protections are there to make serious incidents less likely. Depending on your role, you might only see a handful of worst-case scenarios over a career. I&rsquo;d like to have some practice making decisions under those conditions before I have to do it for real.</p>
        <p>That&rsquo;s why I built my homelab. I use it to explore how attacks unfold, how defences respond, and what traces an attacker&rsquo;s tactics, techniques and procedures leave behind. When an incident is unclear, I want to have a sense of where to start, what evidence to look for, and how to decide what to check next. The lab also gives me room to follow my curiosity across a field where I feel like I&rsquo;ve only scratched the surface.</p>
        <p>My background as a tradie still shapes how I learn. I like getting hands-on, working out why something behaves the way it does, and trying a different angle when the obvious one gets me nowhere. I bring that approach to the lab, and I use this site to document what I tried, what the evidence showed, and what I still have questions about.</p>
        <p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/SLyzzed" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View my GitHub profile</a></p>
      </div>
    </ArchivePanel>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
